# Evidessa Research Cursor rules

- Read `docs/CURSOR_HANDOFF.md`, `docs/SESSION_HANDOFF.md`, `docs/STATUS_MATRIX.md`, `docs/BUILD_REPORT.md` and `CONTRIBUTING.md` before changing behaviour.
- `Evidessa` is the reversible user-facing working brand and `HumanCurrent` is the internal R&D codename. Existing `VitalSignal` package names, protocol routes, signed schemas, audit identifiers and cryptographic aliases are stable technical identities; never mass-rename them without an explicit versioned migration and compatibility plan.
- Treat the repository as simulator-only research software. A visible forecast is permitted only as an explicitly generated, unvalidated simulator fixture whose locked state contains no probability and whose revealed values exactly equal the prospective ledger projection. Do not enable personal-data forecasts, personal collection, clinician monitoring, public release or medical claims without the exact signed evidence gates already defined in the project.
- Preserve fail-closed behaviour: missing, stale, conflicting, implausible, low-quality or unauthorised data must abstain or become an explicit gap; it must never appear normal.
- A person's concern and clinician-authored instructions outrank wearable data and model output.
- Keep signal computation deterministic, versioned and provenance-bound. Every displayed forecast number and explanation fact must be projected from typed sealed estimator/ledger fields; never hand-write numeric model claims. A language model may select reviewed explanation structures only; it may not calculate physiology, invent facts, diagnose, prescribe, alert or change treatment.
- Keep proprietary Samsung AARs, secrets, private endpoints, signing material, health records, device identifiers, APKs, logs and databases out of Git.
- Keep proprietary Samsung SDK types inside their dedicated adapter boundary; translate them into versioned canonical contracts before they enter shared analytics, transport, storage or UI code.
- Add failure-path tests with every behavioural change. Always run `python3 tools/validate_project.py` from a clean tracked-file checkout and `node --test prototype/prototype.test.mjs`. When the pinned Android SDK/AGP are available, also run `./gradlew test lint :phone:assembleDebug :wear:assembleDebug`; otherwise report that Android verification as unexecuted rather than weakening or fabricating the gate.
- Report executed checks separately from unverified Android, Samsung SDK, reference-device, battery, privacy, prospective or clinical evidence.
- Make the smallest reviewable change on a feature branch. Do not weaken a release gate to make a demo, build or test pass.
